course: dictionary
lesson: 351
title: The ant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ant is a very small insect with six legs. Ants live in big, organised groups called colonies, often in nests under the ground. The word can also be used in a joke: «ants in your pants» means someone cannot sit still.
explain: Look for clues in the words around ant. «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge» tells you the ant is small, because it needs a lens to look big. Try your meaning in the sentence: a small insect with six legs fits.
explain: Context also tells you what ants are. «Every insect has 6 legs: ants, beetles, bees, ladybirds and grasshoppers all walk on 6 legs.» Ants are insects, and insects have six legs, so you can use the sentence to check what you know.
fact: An ant is a very small insect with six legs.
fact: Ants live in organised groups called colonies, often in nests under the ground.
fact: A colony has a queen ant, who lays eggs, and worker ants, who find food.
fact: Ants are insects: they have three body parts (head, thorax and abdomen), six legs and two antennae.
fact: Some ants bite or sting, such as fire ants, so look at ant nests but do not poke them.
exercise: «Every insect has 6 legs: ants, beetles, bees, ladybirds and grasshoppers all walk on 6 legs.» How many legs does an ant have? | Two | Four | Eight | *Six
exercise: «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» Why does the ant look huge? | Because it is a giant ant | Because ants grow when they are watched | *Because the glass bends the light | Because the glass has painted it
exercise: Which word names a group of ants that live together? | Herd | *Colony | Pack | Flock
test: Jayden reads, «Ants in your pants.» What does this jokey phrase mean? | *Someone cannot sit still | Someone is hiding ants in their trousers | Someone loves insects | Someone is very clean and tidy
test: In an ant colony, which ants find food? | The queen ant | The eggs | *Worker ants | The nest itself
exam: Which is true about «Some ants bite or sting, such as fire ants»? | *Some ants can bite or sting, so do not poke their nests | Ants only sting in summer | Ants never bite | Fire ants are not ants at all
